WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.575
FormBridge helps restaurant teams turn changing conversations into booking briefs. Let's follow

00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:11.150
a birthday enquiry through the guest assistant and into the staff desk.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.943
Start in the restaurant library. Add the name, city and information your

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:22.086
team has checked. Only approved facts are published to the guest assistant.

00:00:22.086 --> 00:00:26.800
You can share its page or embed it on your website.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:32.721
Guests can ask about the restaurant before making a request. Here, the

00:00:32.721 --> 00:00:37.993
answer uses the opening hours the team approved. Missing information is left

00:00:37.993 --> 00:00:39.750
for staff to answer.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.327
Alex asks for a birthday dinner for five. The assistant gathers the

00:00:45.327 --> 00:00:50.255
date, time and party size. Alex adds contact details and agrees to

00:00:50.255 --> 00:00:53.950
send the request. A reservation has not been made.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.425
The enquiry now appears in the team's inbox. Staff can see the

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:04.250
requested booking details, open the full conversation and decide what needs attention.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:10.767
Ask FormBridge to find guest requests. It suggests the dietary requirement, seating

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:16.633
preference and occasion, each with the customer's own words. Staff chooses which

00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:18.100
suggestions to keep.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.870
Review the restaurant, city, date, time and guest count. Open a detail

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:28.990
to inspect its source, correct anything that needs attention, then approve and

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.550
save the brief to the team.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.888
Give the enquiry an owner, set its priority and add an exact

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:41.575
due time. Leave a note for the team. Reminders appear while the

00:01:41.575 --> 00:01:44.700
desk is open, with overdue escalation for managers.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:50.853
Create a private review link from the saved, approved enquiry. The guest

00:01:50.853 --> 00:01:56.357
can check the booking details and preferences. Staff notes, contact details and

00:01:56.357 --> 00:01:58.650
the full conversation stay private.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:04.329
Alex changes the party size to six. The correction returns to the

00:02:04.329 --> 00:02:09.359
inbox, removes the previous approval and puts the enquiry back in needs

00:02:09.359 --> 00:02:13.550
reply. Staff reviews the updated request before the next handoff.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.814
Link the enquiry to a guest record when you know it belongs

00:02:19.814 --> 00:02:25.429
to that person. Keep useful preferences and history together. Combining duplicate records

00:02:25.429 --> 00:02:27.300
requires a separate confirmation.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:33.481
The connections screen lets you test email and WhatsApp enquiries. Add a

00:02:33.481 --> 00:02:39.013
new message or a follow-up to an existing conversation. Draft a reply,

00:02:39.013 --> 00:02:42.700
check it, then send it within the simulation.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:49.110
For a complete, approved brief, try a booking handoff. Choose a mock

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:54.870
provider, check simulated availability and create a simulated reference. These connections do

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.750
not contact a real booking platform.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:04.060
The team desk brings the work together: requests needing a reply, decisions

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:09.720
under review, due reminders and returning guests. FormBridge keeps the information clear

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.550
while your team makes the decisions.
